> Iceberg lettuce cooks very quickly. The key is high heat and a very short cooking time to retain its crunch while wilting slightly.

== Prepare Ingredients ==

Tear the @iceberg lettuce{1%head} into large, bite-sized pieces. Wash thoroughly and drain well.
Mince the @garlic{3%cloves}.

== Sauce Mix ==

In a small #bowl{}, combine:
- @soy sauce{1%tbsp}
- @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}
- @sugar{½%tsp}
- @water{1%tbsp}

== Stir-fry ==

Heat your #wok{} over high heat. Add @neutral oil{1%tbsp} and the minced garlic. Fry for ~{10%seconds} until fragrant but not browned.

Add the lettuce leaves. Toss rapidly for ~{30%seconds} until they just begin to wilt.

Pour the sauce mixture over the lettuce. Continue to toss for another ~{30%seconds} until the lettuce is coated and the sauce is hot.

== Finish ==

Drizzle with @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}. Give it a final toss and serve immediately to prevent the lettuce from getting soggy.